.TH SDR-UNIVERSAL 1 "" "sdr-universal" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sdr-universal \- rtl_tcp gateway for SDRplay RSP receivers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sdr-universal
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Exposes an SDRplay RSP1B as an rtl_tcp server, so that software written for
RTL-SDR dongles (for example AbracaDABra) can use it, with per-band gain
control, an RF level indication and bandwidth selection.
.PP
The rtl_tcp server listens on TCP port 1234 and a control port (used by
AbracaDABra to compute the RF level) on the next port. By default both listen on
all network interfaces and have no authentication: use \fB\-\-bind\fR and/or a
firewall to restrict access.
.PP
The SDRplay API 3.x is not part of this package and is loaded at run time.
Without it, only the simulated receiver (\fB\-\-mock\fR) can be used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
rtl_tcp port (default 1234). The control port is N+1.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDR"
Listen address for both ports (default 0.0.0.0, all interfaces; same as SDR_BIND).
Use 127.0.0.1 to accept only connections from the local machine.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mdns
Do not advertise the server on the local network (same as SDR_MDNS=0). By default
the rtl_tcp server is advertised as a _rtl_tcp._tcp service (mDNS), unless it listens
on the loopback interface only.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Name shown to clients that discover the server (same as SDR_NAME). Default:
"SDR Universal on <host>".
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Detailed traces (same as SDR_VERBOSE=1).
.TP
.B \-\-mock
Simulated RSP1B, no hardware needed (same as SDR_MOCK=1).
.TP
.BI \-\-mock\-level " DBM"
Simulated antenna level in dBm, default \-75 (same as SDR_MOCK_LEVEL_DBM).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.SH LOGGING
Log lines go to standard error, with a UTC timestamp, the level and the module.
The default level is info; \fB\-\-verbose\fR selects debug. The RUST_LOG
environment variable overrides it, with a global level and/or per-module levels,
for example \fBRUST_LOG=warn\fR or \fBRUST_LOG=info,backend::sdrplay=debug\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter (see LOGGING).
.TP
.B SDRPLAY_API_LIB
Full path of libsdrplay_api.so, instead of the default system search.
.SH SEE ALSO
/usr/share/doc/sdr-universal/README.md and the other files in that directory.
.SH AUTHOR
pbranly, https://github.com/pbranly/sdr-universal
